<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Per-Category Performance Analysis on IndusCP</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An aggregated accuracy score can mask significant performance variations across different problem categories. To provide a more transparent and detailed evaluation, we have broken down the performance of our <span id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ConstraintLLM (w/ ToT)</span> on the IndusCP benchmark by category. To further contextualize these results, we also report the ’External Knowledge Percentage’ for each category in Table <a href="#A5.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Appendix E Per-Category Performance Analysis on IndusCP ‣ ConstraintLLM: A Neuro-Symbolic Framework for Industrial-Level Constraint Programming" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, which is the ratio of problem-code pairs in that category to the entire knowledge base.</p>
</div>
